-<section class="feature" id="limits"><div class="f-text"><span class="pill">Honest limits</span><h2>What it cannot do</h2>
-<ul><li>It was trained on 303 patients from one clinic in the 1980s, all referred for angiography. 97 were women.</li><li>The label is angiographic disease, not future heart attacks.</li><li>AUC is 0.91 (95% CI 0.87 to 0.94) with all 13 inputs and 0.84 (0.79 to 0.88) without the invasive and stress-test inputs.</li><li>It has not been tested prospectively or at another site. A good AUC does not show that using it improves outcomes.</li><li>A low estimate does not rule out disease.</li></ul></div>
-<div class="card"><h3>Not a medical device</h3><p>No regulatory clearance or exemption is claimed. Do not use it for care decisions or with real patient information.</p></div></section>
+<section class="row" id="limits"><h2>Limits</h2><div class="body">
+<ul><li><strong>Small, old data.</strong> 303 patients from one clinic in the 1980s, all referred for angiography. 97 were women.</li><li><strong>The label is angiographic disease,</strong> not future heart attacks.</li><li><strong>Accuracy.</strong> AUC is 0.91 (95% CI 0.87 to 0.94) with all 13 inputs and 0.84 (0.79 to 0.88) without the invasive and stress-test inputs.</li><li><strong>Not validated.</strong> It has not been tested prospectively or at another site. A good AUC does not show that using it improves outcomes.</li><li><strong>A low estimate does not rule out disease.</strong></li><li><strong>Not a medical device.</strong> No regulatory clearance or exemption is claimed.</li></ul></div></section>
